-   * so `cqi` is 1% of the card's content width.
-   *
-   * k_n = 2500 / W_n, W_n being the width in px at 25 px of the widest formatted figure of
-   * n characters (the built app, Plus Jakarta Sans 600, letter-spacing -0.035em,
-   * tabular figures), taken over dot-grouped strings with and without "−" and over grams
-   * ("$ 150.000", "−$ 150.000", "$ 1.500.000" ... "−$ 999.999.999", "1.234,55 g"), floored
-   * to two decimals: the figure then fills at most the card's content width.
-   *
-   *   n   8      9       10      11      12      13      14
-   *   W   98     112.125 126.25  133.375 148.5   162.625 176.75
